{% extends 'base.html.twig' %}

{% block title %} {{ title }}!{% endblock %}

{% block body %}
    <!-- <h1>League Tracker Home Page</h1>  -->
    {% if app.user and is_granted('ROLE_SAMPLE') %}
        <h2>xxxWelcome to Premier Golf League Tracker!</h2>
        <p>
            To see if you might be interested in using this application, take a quick look at list of bullet items below.  If these features
            meet your league requirements, then just contact me at the email address I provide below and provide the information that I require.  I will help you get set 
            up.  There is no cost to League Tracker.  It's here for any league to use free of charge.  
        </p>
        <h2>Feature List</h2>
        <ul>
            <li>Designed specifically for league play, with singles, 2, 3, or 4 person teams, stroke or match play.</li>
            <li>Accomodates both singles and team play as well as special league match events, e.g., scramples, shambles, etc.</li>
            <li>Access to the system is entirely web based, meaning to use League Tracker, you and your league members must have access to the Internet.</li>
            <li style="padding-left: 4em;">League Tracker is Bootstrap enabled.  Meaning that all pages and dialogs in the application are "responsive" and "fit" the size of 
            your screen.  Each page adapt dynamically to the viewport of the device on which they are viewed.  This makes the pages respond, look good, and work reasonably well 
            on phones, tablets, laptops, as well as full screen devices.</li> 
            <li style="padding-left: 4em;">Currently, there are no installable "mobile or tablet apps" for League Tracker. </li>
        </ul>
        <h3>Seasons, Sessions, and Events</h3>
        <ul>
            <li>Players or teams play against each other in a <strong>Season</strong></li>
            <li style="padding-left: 4em;">A <strong>Season</strong> is broken into one or more <strong>Sessions</strong> and <strong>Sessions</strong> 
            contain one or more <strong>Events</strong></li>
            <li style="padding-left: 4em;">The following is an example of a sample league's 2018 season containing 2 sessions and 17 events:</li>
            <li>Players or teams points for each session and the entire season are calculated each week.  For sinlges player points are accumulated sort of like the 
            FedEx Cup point system, where players earn ponts each week for placing in the event from 1st to 10th place.  For match play, points are earned as described in the 
            Scoring section below. </li>
        </ul>
        <img src="{{ docbase }}images/help/season.jpg"/> 
        <h3>Games</h3>
        <ul>
            <li style="padding-left: 4em;">An <strong>Event</strong> consists of <strong>Games</strong> where in each <strong>Game</strong> singles play in stoke play or match play, 
            or one team plays another in match play format, where a team's A player match plays the other team's A player, and a team's B player match plays the other team's 
            B player.</li>
            <li style="padding-left: 4em;">The following is an example of one team match play event in a sample league:</li>
            <li style="padding-left: 4em;">For singles play, an <strong>Event</strong> consists of <strong>Games</strong> where in each <strong>Game</strong> one player plays 
            against another in match play format or players play against all other players in the <strong>Event</strong> in stroke play.  </li>
        </ul>
        <img src="{{ docbase }}images/help/event.jpg"/> 
        <h3>Team/Singles Match Play Scoring</h3>
        <ul>
            <li style="padding-left: 4em;">In match play, if players tie on a hole (after applying the handicap), each player is awarded .5 points.  Winning a hole gives the 
            winner a whole point.</li>
            <li style="padding-left: 4em;">There is one point awarded for low player net.  If players tie low net, each player is awarded .5 points; otherwise, 
            the player with the lowest net is awarded the entire point.</li> 
            <li style="padding-left: 4em;">In team play, there is also one point awarded for low team net.  If teams tie low net, each team is awarded .5 points; otherwise, 
            the team with the lowest net is awarded the entire point.</li> 
            <li style="padding-left: 4em;">The following is an example of an event results in a sample league.  The results also show current standings:</li> 
            <img src="{{ docbase }}images/help/event_results.jpg"/> 
        </ul>
        <h3>Generating a Schedule</h3>
        <ul>
            <li>There is functionality to generate a <strong>Season</strong> and a "round robin" schedule of <strong>Events</strong> 
            based on a number of parameters.  Here is an example of how this functionality works in a sample league:</li>
            <li style="padding-left: 4em;">The 9 hole sample league runs for 17 weeks (first parameter).</li>
            <li style="padding-left: 4em;">The generator splits the 17 weeks into two <strong>Sessions</strong> (another parameter)</li>
            <li style="padding-left: 4em;">The first <strong>Sessions</strong> lasts for 8 weeks.  For the first 7 weeks, teams play each other in a match play format.  
            The 8th week is what is called a "position match", where the team in first place at that time plays the team in second place, the third place team 
            plays the fourth place team, etc., on down the line.</li>
            <li style="padding-left: 4em;">After the 8th events, results are calculated and the team with the highest point total is the 1st half winner.</li> 
            <li style="padding-left: 4em;">The second <strong>Sessions</strong> also lasts for 8 weeks, and also for the first 7 weeks of that session
            teams play each other in a match play format, with the 8th week also being a "position match".</li>
            <li style="padding-left: 4em;">Also after the 8th event of the 2nd half, results for that half are calculated and the team with the highest point 
            for that half is the 2nd half winner.</li>
            <li style="padding-left: 4em;">The 17th week is "playoff match" where the winner of the first half plays the winner of the second half to determine 
            the league champion.  Everyone else plays a 2 person scramble with handicaps.</li> 
        </ul>
        <h3>Handicapping</h3>
        <ul>
            <li>League Tracker uses the World Handicap Formula to determine a player's handicap index and handicap.  It's unofficial, but it works well as any for league play and 
            it gives a player an idea of what their handicap would be if they recorded their scores using an offical USGA site.</li>  League handicaps are separate from the club's USGA
            handicap.  Handicaps are league specific.  If a player plays in multiple leagues, that player has a handicap index and handicap specific to that league.  
            <li style="padding-left: 4em;">The following is an example of one player's handicap page.</li> 
            <img src="{{ docbase }}images/help/handicap.jpg"/> 
        </ul>
        <h3>Other Functionality</h3>
        <ul>
            <li>Most of the other administrator functionality in League Tracker is CRUD based, where you can list, <strong>C</strong>reate, <strong>R</strong>etrieve, 
            <strong>U</strong>pdate, and <strong>D</strong>elete various League Tracker entities.</li>
        </ul>                                    
        <h3>Special Events</h3>
        <ul>
            <li>
                In addition to the weekly league event schedule, League Tracker is also equipped to handle and calculate the results of special team match events.  
                League Tracker currently supports scrambles, shambles, better ball, and low team net formats, with and without adjusting for handicaps.  More details 
                regarding team match events are available in the help section.  
            </li>
        </ul>                                    
        <h2><span id="getting_started">Getting Started</span></h2>
        <p>
            To get started with your league, send an email to 
            <a href="javascript:window.location.href = 'mailto:' + ['League','Tracker'].join('@')">creinke<!---->@<!---->rkm-associates.com</a> 
            and provide the following information:
        </p>
        <ul>
            <li>The name of your league.</li>
            <li>The course that your league plays, including:</li>
                <li style="padding-left: 4em;">The website where the the course scorecard can be found.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
            Generally, within 24 hours, you will receive two sets of trial credentials for your league, administrator credentials and user credentials.
        </p>
    {%  endif %}
    {% if not app.user %}
        <h2>Welcome to Premier Golf League Tracker!</h2>
        <p>
            If you have set up your league already, just log in with either your league's admin or user credentials.
        </p>
        <p>
            If you are here checking out League Tracker, firstly, <strong>it is free to use</strong>!  To get started, you can log in with either the credentials 
            <strong>sample_admin/password</strong> or <strong>sample_user/password</strong>.  This will provide you access to the sample league as either the 
            league's administrator or as a user/member of the sample league respectively.  If you log in as either the sample admin or as a sample user, you will not be able 
            to modify or update any sample league data, but you will have access to all sample league data and most of the user interface dialogs and functionality.  
        </p>
        <p>
            The sample league is a typical after work golf league, where each team consists of 2 players playing 9 holes.  There is an additional sample league
            that works well for teams playing on a golf simulator, that is, 3 player teams playing 18 holes.  The credentials to access the 3 person 18 hole sample 
            league an admin and a member are <strong>sample3_admin/password</strong> and <strong>sample3_user/password</strong> respectively.  
            The purpose of providing two sample leagues is to show you the various functionality that league tracker provides.  
        </p>
        <p>
            Likely the 2, 3, and 4 person per team functionality provided by League Tracker will work for most league play. Some leagues, however, 
            may have different or more unique requirements.  Use the sample leagues to determine if League Tracker meet your leagues requirements.  If additional 
            features are needed, just contact me at <a href="javascript:window.location.href = 'mailto:' + ['League','Tracker'].join('@')">creinke<!---->@<!---->rkm-associates.com</a> 
            and I'll see if I can add those features.  
        </p>        
        <p>
            Click the Help menu item for more details on using League Tracker.  Then log into to one of the sample leagues to see how things work and get more 
            information on how to get going with your league.  
        </p>
    {% endif %}    
{% endblock %}
